U7: 9. If the force on a rocket moving in force free space with an exhaust velocity of gases \( 300 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{sec} \) is 210 N , then the rate of combustion of the fuel, is: (1) 0.7 kg/s (2) \( 1.4 \mathrm{~kg} / \mathrm{s} \) (3) \( 2.7 \mathrm{~kg} / \mathrm{s} \) (4) \( 10.7 \mathrm{~kg} ","For a rocket in force-free space (no external forces), the thrust comes from ejecting mass: \[ F = \dot{m}\, v_e \] So the fuel burn rate (mass flow rate) is \[ \dot{m} = \frac{F}{v_e} = \frac{210}{300} = 0.7 \ \text{kg/s} \] So the correct option is **(1) \(0.7\ \text{kg/s}\)**.",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,2439,64,0.001078,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
