U7: student has to score 50% marks to pass he get 100 and yet fair by 50 marks to maximum marks should be","Let the maximum marks be \(M\). To pass, the student needs \(50\%\) of \(M\), so passing marks \(= \dfrac{M}{2}\). He got \(100\) and failed by \(50\) marks, so passing marks \(= 100 + 50 = 150\). So, \[ \dfrac{M}{2} = 150 \Rightarrow M = 300 \] **Maximum marks \(=\mathbf{300}\).**",Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1953,64,0.000884,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
