U14: Solve the above question",I’m keeping the expansion exact (no rounding). \[ (a+b+c)^2-(a^2+b^2+c^2) \] First expand: \[ (a+b+c)^2=(a+b+c)(a+b+c) \] \[ = a^2+b^2+c^2+2ab+2bc+2ca \] Now subtract \((a^2+b^2+c^2)\): \[ (a^2+b^2+c^2+2ab+2bc+2ca)-(a^2+b^2+c^2)=2ab+2bc+2ca \] So the simplified result is: \[ \boxed{2(ab+bc+ca)} \],Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,2193,64,0.000980,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
