U3: 1km to 600m write the ratio in simplest form",\(1\text{ km} : 600\text{ m}\) 1) Convert to the same unit: \(1\text{ km} = 1000\text{ m}\) So the ratio is \(1000\text{ m} : 600\text{ m} = 1000:600\) 2) Divide both by the GCD \(200\): \[ 1000 \div 200 : 600 \div 200 = 5:3 \] **Simplest form: \(\mathbf{5:3}\).**,Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1790,64,0.000818,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
