033e2200-10ef-41a2-9810-e61d17ad4230,2026-08-16T09:52:27.302Z,1,3,"U1: Prove the following
U2: Prove the following (cosecA-cotA)^2= 1-cosA÷1+cosA
U3: Prove lHS","**LHS** is \[ (\csc A-\cot A)^2. \] Rewrite in terms of \(\sin A,\cos A\): \[ (\csc A-\cot A)^2=\left(\frac{1}{\sin A}-\frac{\cos A}{\sin A}\right)^2 =\left(\frac{1-\cos A}{\sin A}\right)^2 =\frac{(1-\cos A)^2}{\sin^2 A}. \] Now use \(\sin^2 A=(1-\cos A)(1+\cos A)\): \[ \frac{(1-\cos A)^2}{\sin^2 A}",NA,,,,,Academic,,,,1814,64,0.000828,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
