U8: 9×(4-3),(9×4)-3,9×4+3,9×(4+3) second question","I’m keeping it strictly in order of operations (brackets first, then \( \times \), then \(+/-\)). 1) \(9\times(4-3)=9\times 1=\mathbf{9}\) 2) \((9\times4)-3=36-3=\mathbf{33}\) 3) \(9\times4+3=36+3=\mathbf{39}\) 4) \(9\times(4+3)=9\times7=\mathbf{63}\) So in ascending order: **\(9,\ 33,\ 39,\ 63\)**.",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1958,64,0.000886,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
