U4: d. A board \( 3 \frac{5}{16} \mathrm{~cm} \) thick is glued to a board \( 4 \frac{3}{8} \mathrm{~cm} \) thick. What is the combined thickness of the boards?",Add the whole numbers and the fractional parts separately: Whole numbers: \(3 + 4 = 7\) Fractions: \( \frac{5}{16} + \frac{3}{8} = \frac{5}{16} + \frac{6}{16} = \frac{11}{16}\) So the combined thickness is \[ 7 \frac{11}{16}\text{ cm} \] **Answer: \(\mathbf{7 \frac{11}{16}\text{ cm}}\)**,Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1974,64,0.000892,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
