U3: Find the greatest number that will divide 108 143 and 216 without leaving any remainder
U4: Tell me in easy way possible","**The greatest number is \(\mathbf{1}\).** Easy way: - If one number can divide all three, it must also divide the **difference** of two of them. - Take \(216\) and \(108\): \(216 - 108 = 108\). So any common divisor must divide **108**. - Now check with \(143\): \(143\) is **not divisible** by \(2\",Small Talk,,,,,Academic,,,,1764,64,0.000808,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
