U3: π/6,","**If \(\sin x=-\tfrac12\), the reference angle is \(\frac{\pi}{6}\).** Since sine is negative in Quadrants III and IV: \[ x=\pi+\frac{\pi}{6}+2n\pi=\frac{7\pi}{6}+2n\pi \] or \[ x=2\pi-\frac{\pi}{6}+2n\pi=\frac{11\pi}{6}+2n\pi \] So the **general solution** is \[ \boxed{\,x=\frac{7\pi}{6}+2n\pi \qua",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1787,64,0.000817,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
