U3: Parrelal lines","**Parallel lines** are lines in the same plane that **never meet**, even if you extend them forever. They always stay the **same distance apart**. We write it like \(l \parallel m\). If a third line cuts two parallel lines, that third line is called a **transversal**. Then some angle rules become tr",Quiz_request,,,,,Academic,,,,1725,62,0.000789,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm,gate_llm
