U3: Answer A handwritten geometry question asks whether the sum of the interior angles of any polygon is 180 degrees and requests an explanation.","**No. The sum of the interior angles of every polygon is not \(180^\circ\).** For a polygon with \(n\) sides, divide it into triangles. Each triangle has angle sum \(180^\circ\), and an \(n\)-sided polygon can be divided into \(n-2\) triangles. \[ \text{Sum of interior angles}=(n-2)\times 180^\circ ",Procedural,,,,,Academic,,,,1820,64,0.000830,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
