U4: What is the value of this expression when h = -2 and g = 5 3\sqrt{2h^{2}+g}",\(h=-2\) and \(g=5\). First square \(h\): \[ h^2 = (-2)^2 = 4 \] Now plug into the expression \(3\sqrt{2h^{2}+g}\): \[ 2h^2+g = 2(4)+5 = 8+5 = 13 \] \[ 3\sqrt{2h^{2}+g}=3\sqrt{13} \] So the value is **\(3\sqrt{13}\)** (approximately \(3\cdot 3.6055 \approx \mathbf{10.82}\)).,NA,,,,,Academic,,,,1826,64,0.000833,Skipped full rating by Level-1 gate: gate_llm,1,skip,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,gate_llm,gate_llm
