U28: i don't know","**For your tomato question, an easy “another method” is the unitary method (find 1 kg directly).**

Given \(1\frac{1}{2}\text{ kg} = \frac{3}{2}\text{ kg}\) costs 30 rupees.

To get **1 kg**, divide the cost by \(\frac{3}{2}\):

\[
\text{Price of 1 kg} = 30 \div \frac{3}{2}
= 30 \times \frac{2}{3}
= 20
\]

So, **the price of 1 kg tomato is \(\mathbf{20}\) rupees.**

Do you want a method using **ratio/proportion** also?",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Mock / Practice Questions | Image Upload,,,0.9500,16749,272,0.004047,"The bot correctly and thoroughly addresses the user's math questions and practice requests without any factual or procedural errors. The session includes image upload and multiple practice questions, fitting the academic and mock/practice categories. There are no detected failures or user frustration signals.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | multiple_similar_requests | gate_llm,gate_llm
