U9: There is also cosec sec and cot","**Yes — cosec, sec, and cot are the reciprocal (flip) ratios of sin, cos, and tan:**

\[
\csc\theta=\frac{1}{\sin\theta},\qquad
\sec\theta=\frac{1}{\cos\theta},\qquad
\cot\theta=\frac{1}{\tan\theta}=\frac{\cos\theta}{\sin\theta}.
\]

Using the standard exact values:

- For \(30^\circ\): \(\sin 30^\circ=\frac12,\ \cos 30^\circ=\frac{\sqrt3}{2},\ \tan 30^\circ=\frac{1}{\sqrt3}\)
\[
\csc 30^\circ=2,\quad \sec 30^\circ=\frac{2}{\sqrt3},\quad \cot 30^\circ=\sqrt3
\]

- For \(60^\circ\): \(\sin 60^\circ=\frac{\sqrt3}{2},\ \cos 60^\circ=\frac12,\ \tan 60^\circ=\sqrt3\)
\[
\csc 60^\circ=\frac{2}{\sqrt3},\quad \sec 60^\circ=2,\quad \cot 60^\circ=\frac{1}{\sqrt3}
\]

- For \(45^\circ\): \(\sin 45^\circ=\cos 45^\circ=\frac{\sqrt2}{2},\ \tan 45^\circ=1\)
\[
\csc 45^\circ=\sqrt2,\quad \sec 45^\circ=\sqrt2,\quad \cot 45^\circ=1
\]

