U13: Ok,now subtract 49 upon 60 from 75 upon 80","\[
\frac{75}{80}-\frac{49}{60}
\]

First simplify \(\frac{75}{80}\):
\[
\frac{75}{80}=\frac{15}{16}
\]

Now use a common denominator for \(\frac{15}{16}\) and \(\frac{49}{60}\).
LCM of \(16\) and \(60\) is \(240\).

\[
\frac{15}{16}=\frac{15\times 15}{16\times 15}=\frac{225}{240}
\]
\[
\frac{49}{60}=\frac{49\times 4}{60\times 4}=\frac{196}{240}
\]

Subtract:
\[
\frac{225}{240}-\frac{196}{240}=\frac{29}{240}
\]

**Answer: \(\mathbf{\frac{29}{240}}\)**",Procedural,5,5,5,10,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9800,14683,244,0.003599,"The bot correctly answered all user queries with accurate explanations and addressed the images properly. There were no failures in context handling, incorrect answers, or unwanted template pushes. The user showed no signs of frustration or repeated re-asking due to unresolved issues.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
