U3: recombination of spectrum into white light","**Recombination of spectrum into white light is the process of joining the separated colors (VIBGYOR) back together so they overlap and appear white again.** 
When white light passes through a prism, it disperses because different wavelengths bend (refract) by different amounts. If you place a **second prism inverted** (its refracting edge opposite to the first) in the path of the spectrum, it bends each color back by the opposite amount, so the rays **merge again**—and the emerging beam (or the spot on a screen) becomes **white light**.

