U5: I don't know anything 😔","**Compound interest is when you earn “interest on your interest” (the money grows faster over time).** The key idea is: each time interest is added, the new total becomes the starting point for the next time.

**Main formula (compounded \(n\) times per year):**
\[
A = P\left(1+\frac{r}{n}\right)^{nt}
\]
\[
\text{Compound Interest (CI)} = A - P
\]

- \(P\) = starting money (principal) 
- \(r\) = annual interest rate **as a decimal** (so \(10\% = 0.10\)) 
- \(n\) = number of times interest is added each year (1 yearly, 2 half-yearly, 4 quarterly, 12 monthly) 
- \(t\) = time in years 
- \(A\) = total amount after \(t\) years 

**Quick example (yearly):** Suppose \(P=1000\), rate \(=10\%\), time \(=2\) years, yearly compounding (\(n=1\)).
\[
A = 1000(1+0.10)^2 = 1000(1.10)^2 = 1000(1.21)=1210
\]
\[
\text{CI} = 1210-1000 = \mathbf{210}
\]

Tell me one thing to start: **what numbers does your question give (principal \(P\), rate %, time, and “compounded yearly/half-yearly/etc.”)?** If you don’t have a question yet, I can make one for you.",Conceptual,5,5,5,10,Academic | Speech to Text,,,0.9500,13194,252,0.003247,"The conversation fully addresses the user's academic queries with accurate and clear explanations, including stepwise guidance and formula details. There are no bot failures or user dissatisfaction evident, and the flow includes speech-to-text inputs as indicated. Overall, the session is a successful academic help interaction.",0,full_rate,Academic,Concept Explanation,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
