U3: please can you explain it in Malayalam Jeev Jaane Mile living things you don't want to explain in Malayalam please explain in English I not I can't understand it all","**Living things are organized in levels, from smallest to biggest:**

**1) Cell** – the smallest living part of a body. 
Example: a blood cell.

**2) Tissue** – a group of similar cells that do the same job. 
Example: muscle tissue.

**3) Organ** – made of different tissues working together. 
Example: heart, lungs, stomach.

**4) Organ system** – a group of organs working together. 
Example: digestive system (stomach + intestines), breathing system (lungs).

**5) Organism** – one complete living thing. 
Example: one human, one dog, one tree.

**Then bigger groups in nature:**

**6) Population** – many of the same kind living in one place. 
Example: all the cows in one village.

**7) Community** – all different living things in one place. 
Example: cows + dogs + birds + trees in that area.

**8) Ecosystem** – the community **plus** non-living things (air, water, soil, sunlight). 
Example: a pond ecosystem (fish + plants + water + mud + sunlight).

**9) Biosphere** – all living things on Earth.

