- Divisible: Numbers that are multiples of a number are divisible by that number.
- GCD : The product of all the common factors of given numbers is called their GCD.
- LCM: The LCM of given numbers is the product of their common and uncommon prime factors. LCM is the smallest number that is divisible by all the given numbers.
- The product of two numbers is always equar to the product of their GCD and LCM.

