2576f1a2-9e47-4640-af29-2bc8a43e5e44,2026-08-16T14:27:08.836Z,1,3,"U1: Rescue Team recess and emergency message from a ship in the ocean the message does not mention the name of the place but only gives the coordinates Rescue Team races and emergency message from a ship in the ocean the message does not mention the name of the place but only give the coordinates the Rescue Team is able to reach the exact location without any confusion explain how latitude and longitude help identify the location of the ship why are coordinates more lable then place names in such
U2: Rescue Team recess and emergency message from a ship in the ocean the message does not mention the name of the place but only gives the coordinates Rescue Team races and emergency message from a ship in the ocean the message does not mention the name of the place but only give the coordinates the Rescue Team is able to reach the exact location without any confusion explain how latitude and longitude help identify the location of the ship why are coordinates more lable then place names in such situations
U3: Rescue Team Rises and emergency message from a ship in the ocean the message does not mention the name of the place but only give the coordinates the Rescue Team is able to reach the exact location without any confusion explain how latitude and longitude help identify the precise location of the ship why are coordinates more real able place name in such situations","**Latitude and longitude identify the ship’s precise location by giving its “global address” on Earth.** Latitude measures how far **north or south of the Equator** the ship is, and longitude measures how far **east or west of the Prime Meridian** it is. The two values together match one exact point where the latitude line and longitude line cross, so the rescue team can plot it on a map or enter it into GPS and go straight there.

**Coordinates are more reliable than place names in emergencies because:**
- **In the ocean there may be no nearby place name** to refer to.
- **Many place names are repeated or unclear**, but one coordinate pair points to **only one location**.
- **Place names can be misspelled, misheard, or in different languages**, while coordinates are **standard worldwide**.
- **Navigation tools (GPS, ship radar charts, maps) use coordinates directly**, making them faster and more accurate for rescue.",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Speech to Text,,,0.9500,13023,254,0.003235,"The bot correctly and consistently answers the user's repeated question about latitude and longitude without any errors or failures. The user rephrased the question multiple times but did not indicate dissatisfaction or correction, so no failure tags apply. The session is academic with speech-to-text modality and no issues detected.",0,full_rate,Academic,Concept Explanation,near_duplicate_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
