10daf346-da6b-4ce1-84cb-0bd8f9498789,2026-08-16T13:24:03.605Z,1,6,"U1: Solve

A text-based math problem provides the formula IQ = (MA/CA) × 100, where MA is mental age and CA is chronological age, and asks students to solve for the ages of a group of children based on IQ constraints.
U2: Solve

Solve an inequality using the IQ formula IQ = (MA/CA) × 100 to find the range of mental ages for 12-year-old children whose IQ is between 80 and 140.
U3: Solved equation

A handwritten inequality involving percentages and fractions, showing a solved or partially solved equation.
U4: Solve further

