\[
P(a,b),\quad Q(a+3,b+4),\quad R(a-1,b+7),\quad S(a-4,b+3)
\]

Find the length of side \(PQ\):

\[
PQ=\sqrt{[(a+3)-a]^2+[(b+4)-b]^2}
\]

\[
PQ=\sqrt{3^2+4^2}=\sqrt{25}=5
\]

So, the side length of the square is \(5\) units. Therefore,

\[
\text{Area}=(\text{side})^2=5^2=\boxed{\mathbf{25\text{ square units}}}
\]",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,12778,239,0.003181,"The bot correctly solved the user's math problem twice with accurate and complete answers. There were no failures or misunderstandings, and the user did not express frustration or dissatisfaction. The session is a straightforward academic math help with image uploads.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,same_intent_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
