**Common ways an app can accidentally hurt exam prep:**
- **Reading solutions instead of solving first**, so the brain doesn’t get practice.
- **Not doing timed practice**, so speed and accuracy don’t improve.
- **Depending on hints/steps every time**, so independent problem-solving stays weak.
- **Practicing only easy questions**, not the exam-level mix.

**A safer way to use Flexi (or any app):**
- Try the question for **5–10 minutes first**.
- Then ask the app to explain **only the step you got stuck on**.
- After that, solve **2–3 similar questions without help**.
- Do at least **one timed set** regularly and review mistakes.

If you tell me **which exam** (JEE Main, JEE Advanced, school exam, etc.) and **which subject/topic** you’re working on right now, I’ll help you study it in a way that builds real exam skills.",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Specific Named Resource | Speech to Text,,,0.9500,15297,259,0.003730,The bot correctly answered all math division questions and provided detailed explanations without any factual or procedural errors. The user expressed some confusion but did not indicate unresolved issues or bot failures. No bot failures or session pattern issues were detected.,0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
