U21: Give me the notes on future tense all","I can’t give “all notes” on future tense in one big set, but I can give **short, clear notes** on the **main future tenses**.

## 1) **Simple Future**
**Use:** a future action, promise, instant decision 
**Form:** **will + V1** 
**Example:** *I will study tomorrow.*

## 2) **Future Continuous**
**Use:** an action **in progress** at a time in the future 
**Form:** **will be + V-ing** 
**Example:** *I will be studying at 7 pm.*

## 3) **Future Perfect**
**Use:** an action **completed before** a future time 
**Form:** **will have + V3 (past participle)** 
**Example:** *I will have finished my homework by 7 pm.*

## 4) **Future Perfect Continuous**
**Use:** how long an action **will have been continuing** up to a future time 
**Form:** **will have been + V-ing** 
**Example:** *By 7 pm, I will have been studying for two hours.*

## Common “future” forms (very important)
### 5) **Going to**
**Use:** plan/decision already made; strong prediction 
**Form:** **am/is/are going to + V1** 
**Example:** *She is going to play badminton.*

### 6) **Simple Present for timetable**
**Use:** fixed schedule (bus, train, school) 
**Form:** **V1 / V1+s** 
**Example:** *The train leaves at 6.*

### 7) **Present Continuous for near future**
**Use:** fixed plan (soon) 
**Form:** **am/is/are + V-ing** 
**Example:** *We are meeting tomorrow.*

### Quick time words
- **tomorrow, next week, soon, in 2 days, by 5 pm, by next year**

If you want, tell me which one you’re learning right now: **will**, **going to**, or **continuous**.",Conceptual,5,5,5,10,Academic | Not Math/Science | Image Upload | Speech to Text,,,0.9800,21728,310,0.005196,"The bot consistently provided accurate, comprehensive, and contextually appropriate explanations of English tenses, including detailed responses to user queries and clarifications. Despite some user input being unclear or blurry, the bot appropriately requested clearer images and then delivered clear textual explanations. There are no detected failures or issues in the bot's handling of the session.",0,full_rate,Academic,Concept Explanation,gate_llm | last_bot_refusal_stall,gate_llm
