**8) What is feedback? Why is it important?** 
**Feedback** is the response the receiver gives after getting a message (it can be words, actions, or expressions). It is important because it confirms whether the message was understood, helps correct misunderstandings, and makes communication two-way and effective.

**9) What is perspective in communication?** 
**Perspective** is the way a person understands a message based on their experiences, beliefs, knowledge, culture, and feelings. Different people can interpret the same message differently because their perspectives are not the same.

