U5: B^{\nicefrac{D^{+i}}{\dfrac{\lambda ^{-i}}{}c}}","**It looks like your expression is not fully well-formed as written (there’s an empty denominator in \(\dfrac{\lambda^{-i}}{}c\)).** So I can’t simplify it uniquely yet.

If what you meant is
\[
B^{\frac{D^{+i}}{(\lambda^{-i})c}},
\]
then you can rewrite the denominator using \(\lambda^{-i}=\frac{1}{\lambda^{i}}\):
\[
(\lambda^{-i})c=\frac{c}{\lambda^{i}}
\]
so the exponent becomes
\[
\frac{D^{+i}}{c/\lambda^{i}}=\frac{D^{+i}\lambda^{i}}{c}.
\]
That gives
\[
\boxed{\,B^{\frac{D^{+i}\lambda^{i}}{c}}\,}.
\]

