Perimeter:
\[
2(l+b)=92 \;\Rightarrow\; l+b=46
\]

Diagonal:
\[
\sqrt{l^2+b^2}=34 \;\Rightarrow\; l^2+b^2=34^2=1156
\]

Now use \((l+b)^2=l^2+b^2+2lb\):
\[
46^2 = 1156 + 2lb
\]
\[
2116 = 1156 + 2lb
\]
\[
2lb = 960 \;\Rightarrow\; lb=480
\]

So the area \(= l\times b = \boxed{480\ \text{m}^2}\).",NA,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Image Upload | Speech to Text,,,0.9500,13348,259,0.003325,The bot correctly understood and answered the user's math questions with no factual or procedural errors. The session includes speech-to-text and image upload modalities as indicated by metadata. There are no detected failures or user dissatisfaction in the conversation.,0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,same_intent_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
