The student moves:

- \(4\text{ m}\) east
- \(20\text{ m}\) south
- \(20\sqrt{2}\text{ m}\) northwest

A \(20\sqrt{2}\text{ m}\) northwest movement has components:

- \(20\text{ m}\) west
- \(20\text{ m}\) north

So:

- East–west movement: \(20 - 4 = 16\text{ m}\) west
- North–south movement: \(20 - 20 = 0\)

