34bfa9e9-4b50-4341-b196-6dd9f44a0b05,2026-08-16T02:20:49.783Z,1,3,"U1: Ans

A physics problem asks for the electrostatic potential energy of two point charges placed at specified coordinates in an external electric field.
U2: 3. Two wires of same length and same area of cross-section buf made of different material of resistivities \( \rho_{1} \) and \( \rho_{2} \) are connected in series. The equivalent resistivity of the combination is

CBQ (O) CBSE 2026
(a) \( \frac{1}{2}\left(\rho_{1}+\rho_{2}\right) \)
(b) \( \rho_{1}+\rho_{2} \)
(c) \( \sqrt{\rho_{1} \rho_{2}} \)
(d) \( 2\left(\rho_{1}+\rho_{2}\right) \)
U3: Give a more precise ans","**Equivalent resistivity (more precise): \(\displaystyle \rho_{\text{eq}}=\frac{\rho_1+\rho_2}{2}\)**

Because
\[
R_1=\rho_1\frac{L}{A},\quad R_2=\rho_2\frac{L}{A}
\]
\[
R_{\text{series}}=R_1+R_2=(\rho_1+\rho_2)\frac{L}{A}
\]
If you replace them by one uniform wire of **same area \(A\)** and **total length \(2L\)**:
\[
R_{\text{eq}}=\rho_{\text{eq}}\frac{2L}{A}
\]
Equating:
\[
\rho_{\text{eq}}\frac{2L}{A}=(\rho_1+\rho_2)\frac{L}{A}\;\Rightarrow\;
\boxed{\rho_{\text{eq}}=\frac{\rho_1+\rho_2}{2}}
\]

So the correct option is **(a)**.",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,12992,243,0.003223,The bot correctly answered the user's physics and resistivity questions with no evident errors or failures. The session is academic with image uploads but contains no bot failures or user complaints. User sentiment is neutral with no explicit positive or negative feedback.,0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,correction | gate_llm,gate_llm
