U10: question Haryana angiling day angle in the naming angle first chapter listen to me teach me from this chapter any questions from this chapter any question OKay now tell me the answer180of all question","**Not all angles are \(180^\circ\).** Only a **straight angle** is \(180^\circ\), and a **linear pair** adds up to \(180^\circ\).

**Angle naming (first chapter: Lines & Angles) — quick rules**
- \(\angle ABD\): the **middle letter \(B\)** is the vertex. It’s the angle between rays \(BA\) and \(BD\).
- \(\angle BDC\): vertex is **\(D\)**. Angle between rays \(DB\) and \(DC\).
- \(\angle ACB\): vertex is **\(C\)**. Angle between rays \(CA\) and \(CB\).

**When do you write \(180^\circ\)?**
- If \(A, B, D\) are on the **same straight line** (so \(BA\) and \(BD\) are opposite rays), then \(\angle ABD = 180^\circ\).
- If \(B, D, C\) are on the **same straight line**, then \(\angle BDC = 180^\circ\).
- If \(A, C, B\) are on the **same straight line**, then \(\angle ACB = 180^\circ\).

Otherwise, you cannot say \(180^\circ\) without the diagram/given measures.

