**Rule during this period:** each day do **(1) next exam subject + (2) one “later” subject (mostly Maths) + (3) 20–30 min quick revision**.

**From now until 14 Sept (prep phase)**
- **Daily (school day):** 2 blocks of 60–90 min + 20 min recap 
- **Daily (holiday):** 3 blocks of 90 min + 30 min recap 
- **Block 1:** Science (until 15) 
- **Block 2:** Maths (keep Maths running early so it doesn’t pile up) 
- **Block 3 (short):** English/Hindi writing practice alternating days

**Exam-phase schedule (14–26 Sept)**
- **14 Sept (day before Science):** 
Science full revision + diagrams/formulas + 1 sample paper (timed if possible)
- **15 Sept (Science exam):** 
After exam: English (literature + writing formats)
- **16 Sept:** 
English heavy day: 1 reading/grammar set + 2 writing tasks
- **17 Sept (English exam):** 
After exam: Hindi (grammar + writing)
- **18 Sept:** 
Hindi heavy day: writing practice + literature Q/A
- **19 Sept (Hindi exam):** 
After exam: Maths (start past paper / tough chapters)
- **20 Sept:** 
Maths full day: 2–3 chapters + practice questions
- **21 Sept:** 
Maths revision + 1 full sample paper (timed)
- **22 Sept (Maths exam):** 
After exam: Subject for **24th** (tell me which one—SST? Computer? etc.)
- **23 Sept:** 
Prep for **24th** exam (full revision + sample paper)
- **24 Sept (exam):** 
After exam: light IT (definitions, shortcuts, theory)
- **25 Sept:** 
IT full revision + practice questions
- **26 Sept (IT exam):** done

**One smart daily template (use this on prep days)**
- **Block A (90 min):** Next exam subject (highest priority) 
- **Break (10–15 min)** 
- **Block B (75–90 min):** Maths / upcoming subject 
- **Break** 
- **Block C (30–45 min):** Writing/grammar or quick recap + mistakes notebook

