(ii) Calculate the area of the rectangle.","For the rectangle with \(A(-4,1), B(3,1), C(3,6), D(-4,6)\):

(i) **Lengths \(AB\) and \(BC\)** 
Since \(A\) and \(B\) have the same \(y\)-coordinate (\(1\)), \(AB\) is horizontal, so its length is the difference of \(x\)-coordinates:
\[
AB = |3-(-4)| = |7| = \mathbf{7}
\]
Since \(B\) and \(C\) have the same \(x\)-coordinate (\(3\)), \(BC\) is vertical, so its length is the difference of \(y\)-coordinates:
\[
BC = |6-1| = |5| = \mathbf{5}
\]

(ii) **Area of the rectangle** 
\[
\text{Area} = AB \times BC = 7 \times 5 = \mathbf{35}\ \text{square units}
\]

**Final answers:** \(AB=\mathbf{7}\), \(BC=\mathbf{5}\), Area \(=\mathbf{35}\ \text{square units}\).",Procedural,5,5,5,10,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,14243,230,0.003523,The bot correctly and fully answers all user questions with accurate explanations and no failures. The session involves academic math content with image uploads but no evidence of any bot failures or user dissatisfaction.,0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
