U3: Solve it","Start with what you wrote: kinetic energy depends on mass and speed,
\[
KE \propto m^{a}v^{b}\quad \Rightarrow\quad KE = K\, m^{a}v^{b}.
\]

Now use dimensions.

- Dimension of kinetic energy:
\[
[KE]=[\,\text{work}\,]=[F][L]=(M\,L\,T^{-2})(L)=M\,L^{2}\,T^{-2}.
\]
- Dimension of mass: \([m]=M\)
- Dimension of velocity: \([v]=L\,T^{-1}\)

So
\[
[KE]=[K]\,[m]^a[v]^b \Rightarrow M L^{2}T^{-2}= M^{a}(L T^{-1})^{b}=M^{a}L^{b}T^{-b}.
\]

Match powers of \(M, L, T\):

- For \(M\): \(a=1\)
- For \(L\): \(b=2\)
- For \(T\): \(-b=-2\Rightarrow b=2\) (consistent)

So the relation is
\[
\boxed{KE \propto m v^{2}}.
\]

Including the usual constant from mechanics,
\[
\boxed{KE=\frac12 m v^{2}}.
\]",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Image Upload,,,0.9500,13247,249,0.003314,"The bot correctly understood and answered the user's physics dimensional analysis question with no factual or procedural errors. The session included image uploads and the bot appropriately requested clearer images initially, then provided a complete solution. There are no detected failures, so the scores reflect full resolution and reliability with neutral user sentiment.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,same_intent_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
