SETS - RECALL

We help you to revise here the basic set concepts that you have studied in Class VI.
1. The word set is used for a collection of objects of any kind whatsoever, whereby given any object, we can say with certainty whether the object belongs to that collection or not. In other words,

A set is a collection of well defined objects.
The following are some examples of sets:
(i) a set of fruits;
(ii) the set of teachers teaching you;
(iii) the set of letters in the word ""CONSTANT"".

The following are not well defined collections and are, therefore, not sets :
(i) the books that are a fun to read;
(ii) the movies that are good.
2. Sets can be specified by any of the following methods:
(i) Description form
(ii) Tabular form or the Roster form
(iii) Rule method or Set Builder form

NOTATIONS
1. The sets are usually denoted by capital letters \( \mathrm{A}, \mathrm{B}, \mathrm{C} \), etc., and the members of the set are denote
