U6: Explain all the point differently broooo","**A shopping mall is a big indoor market with many stores, food places, and entertainment, and this project starts by introducing the topic and saying what it wants to find out (objectives). It explains the main features of a mall—different shops, branded items, a food court, movie halls, parking, and security. It then talks about malls as hangout places where people come not only to shop but also to meet friends, spend time, and enjoy a “day out.” The project discusses how malls increase buying habits through brands, discounts, ads, and window displays, making shopping feel like a lifestyle (consumer culture). It also explains that malls can show social differences because some people can easily afford things there while others may feel it’s too expensive or not meant for them (class/status). Next, it describes how malls change youth life—fashion trends, eating out more, spending weekends outside, and posting on social media. It includes the work side too: malls provide jobs like sales staff, cleaners, guards, and managers, and it looks at their work hours and behaviour rules. It mentions modern systems like CCTV cameras, digital payments, and apps, which make shopping convenient but also increase monitoring. After that, it explains how malls can affect local shops and street markets—some lose customers while others adjust to compete. It also points out environmental issues like high electricity use (AC, lights), plastic and food waste, and more traffic. Finally, the project ends by summarising the main points in the conclusion, listing sources in the bibliography, and thanking helpers in the acknowledgement.**",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Not Math/Science | Image Upload,,,0.9500,13889,275,0.003411,"The bot provided comprehensive, relevant academic content about sociology and shopping malls, including responding to the image upload. There were no failures such as incorrect answers, context issues, or 