U13: 2. Only numericals and formulas","**Formulas needed for NCERT Class 9 “Motion” numericals (with graph formulas too):**

I’ll keep extra digits in intermediate steps if we calculate, and round only at the end.

**A) Basic quantities**
- **Speed:** \(\displaystyle \text{speed}=\frac{\text{distance}}{\text{time}}\)
- **Average speed:** \(\displaystyle v_{\text{avg speed}}=\frac{\text{total distance}}{\text{total time}}\)
- **Velocity:** \(\displaystyle v=\frac{\text{displacement}}{\text{time}}\)
- **Average velocity:** \(\displaystyle \vec v_{\text{avg}}=\frac{\text{total displacement}}{\text{total time}}\)
- **Acceleration:** \(\displaystyle a=\frac{v-u}{t}\) 
where \(u=\) initial velocity, \(v=\) final velocity, \(t=\) time

**B) Equations of uniformly accelerated motion (SUVAT)**
- \(\displaystyle v=u+at\)
- \(\displaystyle s=ut+\frac12 at^2\)
- \(\displaystyle v^2=u^2+2as\)
- \(\displaystyle s=\frac{(u+v)}{2}\,t\)

**C) Graph formulas**
- **Distance–time graph:** 
\(\displaystyle \text{speed}=\text{slope}=\frac{\Delta s}{\Delta t}\)
- **Velocity–time graph:** 
\(\displaystyle \text{acceleration}=\text{slope}=\frac{\Delta v}{\Delta t}\) 
\(\displaystyle \text{displacement}=\text{area under }v\text{-}t\text{ graph}\)
- If the graph region is a **rectangle:** area \(=vt\)
- If a **triangle:** area \(=\frac12 \times \text{base} \times \text{height}\)
- If a **trapezium:** area \(=\frac12 (u+v)t\)

**D) Units (must in numericals)**
- Distance/displacement: m, km 
- Time: s, h 
- Speed/velocity: m/s, km/h 
- Acceleration: m/s\(^2\)

Send one numerical (photo or typed), and I’ll solve it step-by-step using these formulas.**",Conceptual,5,5,5,10,Academic | Specific Named Resource,,,0.9800,21416,281,0.004929,"The bot consistently provided detailed, accurate, and relevant academic content aligned with the user's requests for class 9 NCERT science chapters. There were no failures such as incorrect answers, context loss, or unwanted template pushes, and the user did not express dissatisfaction or re-ask due to incomplete or incorrect answers.",0,full_rate,Academic,Summary / Notes,explicit_frustration | gate_llm,gate_llm
