U5: Continue the chapter","**Which chapter is it (name/book/board), and what is the next heading on the page?** “Continue the chapter” is too broad for me to do responsibly without knowing the exact section.

If your next section is the usual Class 11 flow after Planck/photon idea, it typically goes to **the photoelectric effect**, and the connection is:

- **Photons carry energy** \(E=h\nu\). 
- A metal needs a **minimum energy** to release an electron (work function \(\phi\)). 
- So emission happens only if 
\[
h\nu \ge \phi
\]
- Any extra energy becomes the electron’s maximum kinetic energy:
\[
K_{\max}=h\nu-\phi
\]

