1. Line \(p\) is perpendicular to line \(l\). 
2. Line \(q\) is perpendicular to line \(m\). 
3. Line \(l\) is parallel to line \(m\). 
4. If two lines are perpendicular to two parallel lines, then those two lines are parallel to each other. 
5. Therefore, \(p\) is parallel to \(q\). 

