A textbook page asks the student to solve Celsius-to-Fahrenheit and Fahrenheit-to-Celsius temperature conversions using the provided formulas.","**The image shows how to convert between Celsius and Fahrenheit.**

**Celsius to Fahrenheit:**

1. Multiply the Celsius temperature by \(\frac{9}{5}\).
2. Add \(32\).

\[
^\circ F=\left(^\circ C\times\frac{9}{5}\right)+32
\]

For example, for \(40^\circ C\):

\[
^\circ F=\left(40\times\frac{9}{5}\right)+32
\]

\[
=72+32=104^\circ F
\]

So, **\(40^\circ C=104^\circ F\)**.

**Fahrenheit to Celsius:**

1. Subtract \(32\).
2. Multiply by \(\frac{5}{9}\).

\[
^\circ C=(^\circ F-32)\times\frac{5}{9}
\]

