\(100^\text{th}\) even \(=2\times100=200\), \(50^\text{th}\) odd \(=2\times50-1=99\) 
\[
200+99=\mathbf{299}\ (\text{option C})
\]

**Difference between the smallest positive integer and the greatest negative integer:** 
\[
1-(-1)=\mathbf{2}
\]

**Uniform velocity question (15 m/s for 10 years):** I’ll keep extra digits in the calculator and round at the end.

Distance \(= vt\). Convert \(10\) years to seconds:
\[
10\times 365\times 24\times 60\times 60 = 315{,}360{,}000\ \text{s}
\]
Now multiply by \(15\ \text{m/s}\):
\[
d = 15 \times 315{,}360{,}000 = \mathbf{4{,}730{,}400{,}000\ \text{m}}
\]
That is
\[
