896a2453-370f-4555-b993-0c6f22b87dd3,2026-08-16T06:26:59.934Z,1,3,"U1: Make a project on the chart paper on the topic of subject verb agreement very beautifully with rules and examples
U2: Create it with proper pictures
U3: Please try to generate in shortcut","**I can’t generate the full chart-paper with pictures for you, but here’s a short “ready-to-copy” version with simple picture ideas.**

**TITLE:** **SUBJECT–VERB AGREEMENT (SVA)** 
**Rule:** Verb matches the subject (singular/plural).

1) **Singular → singular verb** *(Picture: 1 boy)* 
**He plays**. (✓) / He **play**. (✗)

2) **Plural → plural verb** *(Picture: 2 boys)* 
**They play**. (✓) / They **plays**. (✗)

3) **I / You use base verb (no -s)** *(Picture: 2 speech bubbles “I”, “You”)* 
**I read**. **You read**. (✓) / I **reads**. (✗)

4) **A and B → plural verb** *(Picture: 2 kids + “AND”)* 
**Riya and Sita are** here. (✓) / Riya and Sita **is** here. (✗)

5) **Or/Nor → verb matches nearest subject** *(Picture: sign “OR” with 2 arrows)* 
Either Ram or his friends **are** coming. (✓) 
Either his friends or Ram **is** coming. (✓)

6) **Each/Every/Everyone → singular** *(Picture: group + word “EVERYONE”)* 
**Everyone is** ready. (✓) / Everyone **are** ready. (✗)

7) **There is/There are** *(Picture: 1 book vs 2 books)* 
**There is** a book. (✓) / **There are** two books. (✓)

**Tip box:** **He/She/It + verb(-s/-es)**; **I/You/We/They + base verb**.",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Not Math/Science,,,0.9500,13789,257,0.003367,"The bot fully addresses the user's request for a project layout on subject-verb agreement with detailed rules and examples, including picture suggestions. There are no failures or refusals, and the content is accurate and relevant. User sentiment is neutral as there is no explicit positive or negative feedback.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,drop_off | gate_llm,gate_llm
a9212bfc-1dd1-4042-bd19-273bacb5df13,2026-08-16T06:26:50.847Z,29367418,3,"U1: Determine the prime factorisation of 840 .
