U9: PREFACE

The study of mathematics caters to a wide range of interests and abilities. It nurtures imagination, sharpens logical and analytical thinking, and encourages problem-solving skills. Mathematics challenges learners with complex structures and unsolved problems, yet also drives towards simplification-finding the right concepts and methods to make difficult ideas easier to understand, and explaining why things are the way they are.
The Mathematics coursebook series for Classes 1 to 8 has been thoughtfully designed to provide precise, structured, and learner-friendly knowledge of the subject. Developed in accordance with the National Education Policy (NEP) 2020, the National Curriculum Framework (NCF) 2023, and the guidelines of CBSE and other educational boards, these books have been written by expert authors in collaboration with experienced teachers.
Key features of the series:
- Developed to meet the aims and objectives of concept-based teaching competency development.
- Organised in a logical and psychologically appropriate sequence for learners' age and ability.
- Richly illustrated with clear diagrams and figures to aid visual understanding.
- Presented in simple, comprehensible language for easy grasp of concepts.
- Encourages self-study, self-reliance, and confidence in problem-solving.
- Promotes analytic-synthetic, inductive-deductive, heuristic, and problemsolving approaches in teaching and learning.
We believe this series will not only strengthen mathematical understanding but also inspire curiosity, independent thinking, and logical reasoning, enabling learners to become confident problem-solvers and responsible citizens in a global context.

Publishers
