- **Holds leaders accountable:** People can question leaders and highlight public problems (roads, water, corruption). 
- **Encourages participation:** It can motivate voting, discussions, and peaceful campaigns.

## B) How social media can weaken democracy if used irresponsibly

- **Fake news spreads quickly:** People may believe wrong information and vote based on lies. 
- **Hate speech and harassment:** It can silence others and create fear, so free discussion reduces. 
- **Polarization:** People may only follow one side, causing more division and less cooperation. 
