U3: how to do conversion of temperature like Celsius to Kelvin like that you give all formulas","**All the main temperature conversion formulas**

- **Celsius → Kelvin:** \(\;K = {^\circ\text{C}} + 273.15\) 
- **Kelvin → Celsius:** \(\;^\circ\text{C} = K - 273.15\)

- **Celsius → Fahrenheit:** \(\;^\circ\text{F} = \left(\frac{9}{5}\right)\,^\circ\text{C} + 32\) 
- **Fahrenheit → Celsius:** \(\;^\circ\text{C} = \left(\frac{5}{9}\right)(^\circ\text{F} - 32)\)

- **Kelvin → Fahrenheit:** \(\;^\circ\text{F} = \left(\frac{9}{5}\right)(K - 273.15) + 32\) 
- **Fahrenheit → Kelvin:** \(\;K = \left(\frac{5}{9}\right)(^\circ\text{F} - 32) + 273.15\)

**Small note:** Kelvin is written as \(K\) (no degree sign). In some school problems they use \(273\) instead of \(273.15\) for quick answers.",Conceptual,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic | Speech to Text,,,1.0000,12892,288,0.003237,"The bot provided accurate and complete temperature conversion formulas in all turns without any failures or misunderstandings. The user re-asked but did not indicate dissatisfaction or correction ignored, so no failure tags apply. The session is a straightforward academic Q&A with speech-to-text input in the last turn.",0,full_rate,Academic,Concept Explanation,same_intent_reask | paraphrase_reask | multiple_similar_requests | gate_llm,gate_llm
