24a244ab-5c82-4eac-96bd-744bb338527b,2026-08-16T01:55:31.915Z,30785171,3,"U1: Find the trigonometric function of the following angles -90°
U2: Find the trigonometric function of the following 360°
U3: Find the trigonometric function of the following angles -90° with figure","**\(-90^\circ\)** lands on the **negative \(y\)-axis** on the unit circle, so the terminal point is \((0,-1)\).

Using \(\sin\theta = y\) and \(\cos\theta = x\):

\[
\sin(-90^\circ)=-1,\qquad \cos(-90^\circ)=0
\]
\[
\tan(-90^\circ)=\frac{\sin(-90^\circ)}{\cos(-90^\circ)}=\frac{-1}{0}\ \text{undefined}
\]
\[
\csc(-90^\circ)=\frac{1}{\sin(-90^\circ)}=-1,\qquad 
\sec(-90^\circ)=\frac{1}{\cos(-90^\circ)}\ \text{undefined}
\]
\[
\cot(-90^\circ)=\frac{\cos(-90^\circ)}{\sin(-90^\circ)}=\frac{0}{-1}=0
\]

**Figure (description):** Draw the \(x\)- and \(y\)-axes, then draw a circle of radius \(1\) centered at the origin. Start at \((1,0)\) on the positive \(x\)-axis (that’s \(0^\circ\)). Rotate **clockwise** \(90^\circ\) to reach the bottom point of the circle at \((0,-1)\). Mark that point and label it \(-90^\circ\).",Procedural,5,5,3,8.666666666666668,Academic,,,0.9500,12898,242,0.003193,"The bot correctly answered all user queries about trigonometric functions at specified angles with accurate mathematical explanations and no failures. There were no indications of user frustration or repeated corrections, and no bot failures were detected. The session is a straightforward academic math Q&A with no modality or flow markers present.",0,full_rate,Academic,Homework / Assignment Help,same_intent_reask | paraphrase_reask | gate_llm,gate_llm
